;; Tími NOW — DNS zone for timinow.pet
;;
;; Import: Cloudflare dashboard -> timinow.pet -> DNS -> Records -> Import and Export
;;         -> Import DNS records -> upload this file.
;;
;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;; READ THIS FIRST — Cloudflare imports every record as DNS-only (grey cloud).
;;
;; The Clerk records below MUST stay DNS-only (grey cloud). Proxying them breaks
;; Clerk's Frontend API and sign-in fails.
;;
;; The application hostnames are NOT in this file — they are Cloudflare Custom
;; Domains, created by `wrangler deploy`. See the Workers section below.
;;
;; `./scripts/check-dns.sh` verifies the result.
;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

$ORIGIN timinow.pet.
$TTL 300

;; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ Cloudflare Workers ══
;;
;; Nothing to add here. The six application hostnames —
;;
;;     timinow.pet   www   app   providers   admin   voice
;;
;; are Cloudflare **Custom Domains**, declared in the `routes` block of each
;; wrangler config. `wrangler deploy` creates the DNS record and provisions the
;; certificate itself.
;;
;; IMPORTANT: a Custom Domain cannot be created if a record already exists at
;; that hostname. An earlier version of this file shipped placeholder AAAA
;; records pointing at 100:: — if you imported that version, DELETE those six
;; records before deploying, or Cloudflare will refuse the hostname.
;;
;; Deliberately not Routes. A Route needs a proxied placeholder record to exist
;; first, which is a second thing to get right and fails silently when it is
;; not: the hostname resolves to the discard prefix and the request simply
;; hangs.

;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Clerk ══
;;
;; Authentication. Every target below is INSTANCE-SPECIFIC — replace
;; <instance> with the value Clerk shows under Domains in your production
;; instance. Clerk will not verify the domain until these resolve.
;;
;;   DNS-ONLY (grey cloud) — all five. Proxying these breaks sign-in.

clerk                   300  IN  CNAME  frontend-api.clerk.services.
accounts                300  IN  CNAME  accounts.clerk.services.

;; The three below are what let one-time codes arrive from timinow.pet rather
;; than from a Clerk address a veterinary practice will not recognise.
;;
;; They are COMMENTED OUT on purpose: their targets contain an instance id that
;; only your Clerk dashboard knows, and importing them with a placeholder would
;; create three broken records. Clerk shows the exact values under
;; Domains -> DNS records. Uncomment, substitute, and import again — or just add
;; those three by hand, which is usually quicker.
;;
;; clkmail              300  IN  CNAME  mail.<instance>.clerk.services.
;; clk._domainkey       300  IN  CNAME  dkim1.<instance>.clerk.services.
;; clk2._domainkey      300  IN  CNAME  dkim2.<instance>.clerk.services.

;; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Email ══
;;
;; This file once published `v=spf1 -all` — a hard fail, correct at the time,
;; because nothing sent from the apex. That changed when the blog's subscription
;; confirmations started going out through MailerSend, and the record below is
;; what the zone actually carries now. If you re-import an older copy of this
;; file you will silently un-authorise every email the product sends.
;;
;; `~all` rather than `-all`: soft fail while MailerSend is the only sender and
;; DKIM is not yet published. Tighten to `-all` once the DMARC reports are
;; clean and the DKIM record below exists.

@                       300  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 include:_spf.mailersend.net ~all"

;; ── DKIM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;
;; NOT YET PUBLISHED. SPF says a host is allowed to send as this domain; DKIM
;; signs the message itself, and it is the signal large mailbox providers
;; actually weigh. Without it the mail still arrives — with one fewer reason to
;; be believed, and with DMARC able to align on SPF alone.
;;
;; Commented out for the same reason as Clerk's three above: the value is a
;; public key MailerSend generates on their side, and importing a placeholder
;; would create a broken record that looks present. MailerSend prints the exact
;; selector and value under Domains -> DNS records. The selector is usually
;; mlsend2._domainkey; some accounts get a CNAME instead of a TXT.
;;
;; Add it with the exact values rather than by hand:
;;
;;     node scripts/dns-records.mjs \
;;       --dkim-name=mlsend2._domainkey --dkim-value="k=rsa; p=<public key>"
;;
;; mlsend2._domainkey   300  IN  TXT    "k=rsa; p=<public key from MailerSend>"

;; DMARC starts at p=none deliberately. Jumping straight to reject without ever
;; reading a report is how legitimate mail silently disappears. Watch the
;; reports for a fortnight, then tighten to quarantine and then reject.
_dmarc                  300  IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:1morecruise@gmail.com; ruf=mailto:1morecruise@gmail.com; fo=1; adkim=r; aspf=r; pct=100"

;; No inbound mail. Delete this and add MX records if you ever want a mailbox
;; at timinow.pet; the null MX is what tells senders not to bother trying.
@                       300  IN  MX     0 .

;; ═════════════════════════════════════════ Search-engine verification ══
;;
;; NOT YET PUBLISHED, and not required — the site is verifiable without either
;; of these. src/verification.js serves Google's meta tag or file and Bing's
;; meta tag and /BingSiteAuth.xml straight from the Worker, which is enough for
;; a URL-prefix property at https://timinow.pet, and that prefix covers the
;; whole crawlable surface now that the blog lives at timinow.pet/blog.
;;
;; The records below buy one extra thing: a DOMAIN property, which is the only
;; kind Google will verify by DNS and the only kind that reports on every
;; subdomain and scheme at once — providers., admin. and app. in the same view.
;; Worth having eventually; not worth blocking on.
;;
;; Both tokens are issued per-property to an authenticated account and cannot
;; be derived from anything in this repository. Google's DNS token is also a
;; DIFFERENT string from its meta-tag token — swapping them verifies nothing
;; while looking entirely correct.
;;
;;     node scripts/dns-records.mjs --google=<token> --bing=<token>
;;
;; @                    300  IN  TXT    "google-site-verification=<token>"
;; <token>              300  IN  CNAME  verify.bing.com.

;; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ Certificate authority ══
;;
;; Only these CAs may issue for timinow.pet. Cloudflare Universal SSL uses
;; Google Trust Services and Let's Encrypt; Clerk uses Let's Encrypt. The rest
;; are here so a future vendor does not fail issuance mysteriously — remove any
;; you are confident you will never use.

@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "pki.goog"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "digicert.com"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "sectigo.com"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "ssl.com"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issuewild "pki.goog"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issuewild "letsencrypt.org"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 iodef "mailto:1morecruise@gmail.com"
